#
# Targets: research/pilots/zzv2-lam/run_zzv2.py + research/pilots/zeta23e/run_zeta23e.py (base = worktree agent-09 @ 53c1548 disk state;
# zzv2 sha256(16) e202c9d694fa3e1b, zeta23e sha256(16) 6ca8279b7a96af55 — re-base if lanes touch the runners before application).
# Fixes: (a) taskset -c 0,1 lake build ... — hard-caps the build phase at the SPEC's 2 CPUs (the measured build-phase
#        CPU-burst OVER class: zeta23e-p0-run1.log:19-25 OVER=13; lake sizes parallelism from nproc=18 — AGENTS §5 nproc trap;
#        -j does not exist at this toolchain; taskset is A3's empirically-verified working form, function-body only, layer sharing intact);
#        (b) cache retry raised to the full iter4-donor-unblock-plan §5b budget (<=4 attempts) + DEFER-infra verdict on exhaustion
#        (abort=defer per §8 cards 8-9; seed fallback deliberately NOT wired — porting _seed_mathlib into donor-tree runners is out of scope);
#        (c) modal_telemetry path resolution: __file__-relative first (in-repo runs), canonical absolute path as staged-run fallback (§5a gap-2 class).
# Apply from repo root: patch -p1 < research/feasibility/probe/runner-fixes-wave2.patch
# Verified 2026-11-17 by lane A8 (both revisions): dry-run clean + applies clean to fresh copies of both originals; patched files py_compile OK.

